{"author":{"id":"1f592c0ac5a83ec8bdb9b8574bd8dddf2082ee3c98ad9608c7b89c82d05faf99"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792887227,"nonce":"SV2pJJhfnM9YrH9QDZR3okE0nT4=","title":"Pin x-idl by git revision","message":"xavi took x-idl as `path = \"../x-idl\"`, while xwindow and xgpu pin it by git\nrevision. The path form builds against whatever the sibling checkout holds:\nhere it held 753610f while release-sources.json still recorded bf1ab2f, so\ndevelopment builds and release packages used different generators.\n\nPin `x_idl` by `rev` in Cargo.toml at the revision release-sources.json\nrecords, and have the release scripts refuse a mismatch. A local checkout is\npatched in with `[patch.\"https://github.com/rayzor-blade/x-idl.git\"]`.\n\nThe SDK keeps building offline and `--locked` from the x-idl it bundles: the\npacker appends that patch to the SDK's Cargo.toml and drops x-idl's git\n`source` line from the SDK's Cargo.lock (cargo rewrites the lock otherwise,\nand CI's SDK smoke test runs with `--locked`).\n\nFound while testing: `sources()` swept every file under an entry with rglob,\nincluding git-ignored build output. An x-idl checkout with a built\n`tests/node-addon/target` put `x-idl/tests/node-addon/target/...` into the SDK\nand failed `test_sdk_is_reproducible_and_contains_relocatable_sources`. The SDK\nnow takes its files from `git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard`.","files":null}]}